======================================================================
THREAD G: Mode B recursion — how |Z_n| grows as n increases by 2
======================================================================

Mode A: n → n+1: adds m → m + (n-1) = C(n-1,2) + (n-1) = C(n,2) new tile set size.
Mode B: n → n+2: adds m → m + 2(n-1) + 1 = C(n+1,2) - C(n-1,2) + ... tiles.

Actually: m(n) = C(n-1,2). So:
  m(n+1) - m(n) = (n-1)   [Mode A adds n-1 tiles]
  m(n+2) - m(n) = (2n-1)  [Mode B adds 2n-1 tiles]

|Z_n| = F_{m(n)+2}.
Mode A: F_{m+2} → F_{m+n+1}.  [multiply F_{m+2} by ≈ φ^{n-1}]
Mode B: F_{m+2} → F_{m+2n+1}. [multiply F_{m+2} by ≈ φ^{2n-1}]

  n | m=C(n-1,2) | F_{m+2} | Mode-A step |  Mode-B step
   2 |         0 |       1 | +0 tiles | +0 tiles
   3 |         1 |       2 | +1 tiles | +1 tiles
   4 |         3 |       5 | +2 tiles | +3 tiles
   5 |         6 |      21 | +3 tiles | +5 tiles
   6 |        10 |     144 | +4 tiles | +7 tiles
   7 |        15 |    1597 | +5 tiles | +9 tiles
   8 |        21 |   28657 | +6 tiles | +11 tiles
   9 |        28 |  832040 | +7 tiles | +13 tiles
  10 |        36 | 39088169 | +8 tiles | +15 tiles

